###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - CGCNN predicts crystal properties from the crystal graph; it has no force output in this paper. It appears in the registry because later papers use it as an energy/force baseline.
# - The errors are in eV/atom, which has no unit individual; mlips:hasUnit is omitted and the unit is in the labels. The validation MAEs (0.108 and 0.039 eV/atom) used for model selection are not encoded separately.
# - Hyperparameters are in the Supplemental Material (Table S1), which is not part of the version read; none is encoded.
# - The DFT settings of the Materials Project data and of the perovskite database are not described in this paper.
# - No derivation from an earlier registry method is stated.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/xie2018.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

